  "limitations": [
    "Managed identity configuration was written only by the harness to an isolated Hermes profile. Production installer transactions, ownership, diagnostics and UI activation are not integrated.",
    "Native enrollment evidence uses the real Hermes CLI and SIQ pre_tool_call without a session observer or manually issued Intent. Model and operator are synthetic.",
    "The permission envelope represents an instance Grant, not trusted task purpose or actual loaded Skill content. Multi-Skill attribution remains incomplete.",
    "Legacy nonreserved subjects retain existing global-credential behavior. OpenClaw does not yet use the new instance identity enrollment.",
    "The 14-check OpenClaw regression uses a separately built candidate before the final Hermes-only localhost pin; its distinct hash is retained.",
    "The final candidate passes new native enrollment (10 checks), scoped product self-check (7) and legacy Hermes read-only Grant regression (7). Revoked managed calls produce unsigned local pending denials, not signed service receipts.",
    "Only Linux arm64 runtime tested; four cross-builds do not prove native Windows/macOS support, ACL enforcement, same-UID isolation, or WorkBuddy integration.",
    "No Web source changed or new activation browser journey tested. UX-007 and the complete personal/LAN goal remain active. No commit, push, or release."
  ],
